     category: 'styles',
     description: 'Discover cursive lettering styles for tattoo design inspiration. Bold script, elegant cursive, and calligraphy-style Unicode characters for your next ink idea.',
     content: 'Tattoo lettering is a specialized craft — tattoo artists hand-draw each piece to fit the body\'s contours, and no Unicode character can replace that artistry. But Unicode script letters (𝒶𝒷𝒸𝒹 and 𝓪𝓫𝓬𝓭) can help you explore cursive tattoo styles before you sit down with your artist.\n\nThe bold script variant (𝓪𝓫𝓬𝓭) is the closest Unicode gets to the thick-and-thin contrast of a traditional script tattoo — the kind used for names, dates, and single-word pieces. The regular script (𝒶𝒷𝒸𝒹) reads lighter and more delicate, fitting for fine-line or minimalist tattoo styles. Fraktur (𝔥𝔢𝔩𝔩𝔬) covers the Old English / gothic tattoo tradition, one of the most enduring lettering styles in tattoo history.\n\nTattoo artists typically redraw the lettering by hand rather than stenciling from a font. Use this tool to find the general style direction, then bring your favorites to a consultation. The artist will build on your reference with their own expertise on size, placement, and how the lettering follows your body\'s curves.',
