     metaDescription: 'Make your text bigger and bolder with Unicode. Bold, fullwidth, and squared characters for large, attention-grabbing text. Free big font generator.',
     category: 'styles',
     description: 'Make your text look bigger and bolder using Unicode characters. Bold, fullwidth, and squared styles create the visual impression of large, expanded lettering.',
     content: 'Making text look bigger in Unicode is an optical illusion — the character size itself is fixed by the rendering font, but certain character sets fill more horizontal and vertical space than regular letters. Fullwidth characters (ａｂｃｄ) occupy exactly twice the width of standard ASCII characters. They were designed for CJK (Chinese-Japanese-Korean) typesetting systems where each character sits in a uniform square cell, but in a Latin text context, they read as stretched-out, expanded lettering.\n\nSquared characters (🅰🅱🅲🅳) add enclosure around each letter, which increases the total visual footprint of the text. Bold mathematical characters (𝐚𝐛𝐜𝐝) increase the stroke weight, making each letter feel heavier and more commanding. Combining all three — writing in bold fullwidth squared — creates the maximum visual size available within Unicode.\n\nThe result is text that draws the eye before the surrounding content. It is the Unicode equivalent of raising your voice, which is why bold and fullwidth styles are so popular for headlines, announcements, and emphasis in plain-text environments.',
